    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that just feels like another way to stall. if the end result is always the same... just nothingness. it feels like we're all just trapped in this loop of needing to 'feel' something to justify the pain. if nothing truly matters, then shouldn't the most logical thing be to just... stop? to stop fighting against the inevitable? it seems like there's more peace in just letting go than in trying to make sense of a void.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
